# Licensing

This repository contains two distinct kinds of material, and they are licensed
differently. Read this file before reusing anything here.

## 1. Structure and tooling — MIT

The following are released under the MIT licence (full text below):

- this README, this licensing notice, and any other documentation written for
  this repository;
- the JSON schema and file conventions of the files under `daily/` — that is,
  the shape of the data (field names, types, ordering rules, the
  `daily/latest.json` plus `daily/YYYY-MM-DD.json` archive layout);
- any scripts or configuration added to this repository.

You may reuse that structure, schema and documentation freely, including
commercially, provided the copyright notice below is retained.

## 2. Feed content — third-party rights reserved

The excerpts under `daily/` are **not** covered by the MIT licence and are
**not** the copyright of the repository owner.

Every item is a short quotation of a post published on X by a third party,
stored together with a link to the original and machine-generated study
material (translation summaries, vocabulary glosses, comprehension
questions). The source accounts include, among others:

- **Media:** RFI, Le Devoir, Radio-Canada Info, TV5 Monde Info, Le Temps,
  franceinfo, RTBF Info, Les Echos, Le Journal de Montréal, TVA Nouvelles
- **Government and international:** IRCC (`CitImmCanFR`), Statistics Canada
  (`StatCan_fra`), United Nations (`ONUinfo`, `ONU_fr`), OIF
  (`OIFrancophonie`), UNESCO (`UNESCO_fr`)
- **Science and culture:** Sciences et Avenir, CNES, CEA, Ministère de la
  Culture (`MinistereCC`), BnF (`laBnF`)

Copyright in each quoted post remains with its author or publisher. The
quotations are stored and redistributed here for language-study and
commentary purposes, and each item links back to its source. **No licence is
granted by this repository to reuse that third-party text for any other
purpose.** If you want to republish, translate or build on the quoted content
itself, you must clear that with the original rights holder.

Government of Canada content is subject to the
[Crown Copyright](https://www.canada.ca/en/transparency/terms.html) terms;
material from Radio-Canada, RFI, TV5 Monde, Le Devoir, Le Temps and similar
outlets is subject to each outlet's own terms of use.

Machine-generated summaries, translations, glosses and questions in this
repository were produced automatically and are offered under the same terms as
the quoted text they accompany — they are study aids, not authoritative
translations, and should not be relied on as legal or official renderings.

## 3. Trademarks and attribution

Account handles, publication names and logos referenced in the data remain the
trademarks of their owners. Their appearance here is nominative: it identifies
the source of a quotation and does not imply endorsement or affiliation.

